{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch1uhht828ZdFXQBDAZ4Q", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I'm not signing off. I found one confirmed bug and have one open issue I could not get the developer to accept, so the sweep is not finished.\n\n**Filed and confirmed**\n- **Media tab, Videos filter, blank state:** with the Videos filter active and no videos, the caption reads \"No photos found\" while the badge says \"Videos\". This fits the changed blank-state caption that is now built from one constant string.\n\n**Filed but not reproduced by the developer**\n- **Albums, duplicate album:** after trashing both photos and restoring them together (Trash → select both → Restore selected), the Albums tab shows two \"IrisSeed\" tiles, each \"1 items\" (covers huge.jpg and big.jpg), instead of one album with 2 items. I saw it twice, and it persisted after leaving and returning to Albums. The developer replied \"could not reproduce with the steps given.\" The duplicate appeared in my second cycle, after restoring both at once. In the first cycle I restored one photo at a time and did not see it.\n- **Albums, landscape overlap:** the bottom navigation bar covers the second album tile's caption. The developer also could not reproduce this.\n\n**Checked and looked correct**\n- Trash order: items sort newest-first by trashed time. I checked this with several trash/restore sequences, and the order held after rotation.\n- Album covers update when the cover photo is trashed or restored.\n- Restore, Clear selection, and Empty Trash → Cancel all behave correctly, and the Trash empty state appears.\n- Media, Albums, and Library counts agree with each other.\n\n**Not covered**\n- The album detail header cover, the thumbnail cache, and the Media blank-state caption (the Videos case is what I reproduced).\n- Search, Sort, and Favorites beyond their blank state.\n- Two minor items I did not file: \"1 items\" pluralization throughout, and \"1 items moved to Trash\" in the snackbar.\n\n**Data state**\n- Both photos are back in the gallery (Media shows huge.jpg and big.jpg). The Trash is empty.\n- The Albums tab currently shows the two IrisSeed tiles described above.\n\nThe next step is the duplicate album. The developer could not reproduce it from the steps I gave. It might depend on the trash order, so a tester who starts from a clean album could check whether it is a real defect."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 2056, "cache_read_input_tokens": 116003, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 2056}, "output_tokens": 4, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "ad34c2cb-108d-4f69-ab12-b83148095f20", "uuid": "4121ea35-5657-4961-a99a-237211795867", "timestamp": "2026-11-14T00:55:32.232Z", "request_id": "req_011Ch1uhhXYX1LSNFnaGd36e"}
